WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.034
Why did every note system fail?

00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:05.516
One job gets dropped after two weeks.

00:00:05.616 --> 00:00:08.358
Capture, connect, or answer?

00:00:09.558 --> 00:00:16.510
A second brain does three jobs. Capture. Connect, the one humans stop doing.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.300
Answer, with sources we can open. Unconnected notes are a folder.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.552
We save, and almost never go back.

00:00:25.602 --> 00:00:28.648
Four hundred unread items is a debt we avoid looking at.

00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:31.658
The fix is removing the step we keep failing at.

00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:39.678
The AI maintains the wiki, and we read it. Three operations: ingest, lint, query.

00:00:40.228 --> 00:00:46.474
RAG does the work at query time, every time. A wiki does it once, at ingest.

00:00:46.524 --> 00:00:48.658
So understanding accumulates.

00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:55.124
Week one feels like a folder. By weeks two to four, first connections.

00:00:55.174 --> 00:00:59.277
By month three, it beats rereading. By month six,

00:00:59.327 --> 00:01:02.006
it knows things we do not remember learning.

00:01:02.556 --> 00:01:08.994
That's chapter one, concepts. Start with page one: What a second brain actually is.
